        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Calcification"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(incapacitation, primal, transmutation)\n\nA peck from a cockatrice hardens the flesh of the creature struck. The target must succeed at a 20 Fortitude save or become slowed 1 (or slowed 2 on a critical failure). Further failed saves against calcification increase the slowed condition. Once a creature's actions are reduced to 0 by calcification, that creature becomes petrified.\n\nEvery 24 hours after it was petrified, the victim can attempt a 20 Fortitude save to recover. On a success, it becomes flesh again, but is slowed 1 for the next 24 hours. On a critical success, the creature recovers and isn't slowed. On a failure, the creature remains petrified, but can try again in 24 hours. On a critical failure, the petrification is permanent, and the creature can't attempt any more saves."
            },
